      "summary": "Extend the existing candidate refresh and recovery path to replay only proven Goal changes onto an exact observed target. Preserve target-based Round creation, historical attempts, current Skill semantics, exact-candidate checks and fenced publication. Implement on pinned Round 2, selectively adapting useful Round 1 mechanisms.",
      "checklist": [
        {
          "id": "P1",
          "description": "Add shared lineage validation before Plan and Implement launch or resume. Observe managed workspace identity, actual branch/HEAD, cleanliness, unfinished Git operations, recorded base/candidate, declared target tip, attempt authority and planning/Skill context. Verify newly created HEAD equals its declared start; preserve the original base when reopening existing work. Retain observations and reject stale bindings before automated edits. Any workflow-managed repair must precede the observational Plan invocation; changed context requires a fresh invocation without rewriting completed artifacts.",
          "verification": [
            "Extend round_base tests for fresh creation while the shared checkout is on develop, missing-worktree recreation, committed and dirty resumes, branch/HEAD mismatch and stale planning context."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P2",
          "description": "Define an explicit lineage decision using existing Round, planning, handoff and Git evidence. Accept a replay boundary only when clean pre-edit observations and candidate receipts identify a unique Goal-owned change range, including inherited changes from identified source Rounds. Corroborate exact objects, ancestry and continuity; preserve the original recorded base separately from the proven replay boundary. A merge base, branch name, commit author, path filter or clean rebase cannot establish ownership. Missing or contradictory evidence, unexplained commits and ambiguous merge mainlines must retain diagnostics and use supported recovery without importing that history.",
