            "Test a wrong recorded base with an unchanged target and a proven actual starting commit.",
            "Test divergent develop history containing unrelated commits: replay only changes after the proven Goal boundary; preserve everything when that boundary is unavailable or contradictory.",
            "Test unavailable objects, shallow history and merge commits without an explicit proven replay interpretation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P3",
          "description": "Extend the shared Git capability to replay the proven range onto one exact target SHA in a managed workspace. Selectively adapt Round 1's detached replay and journal approach, removing its merge-base ownership assumption and automatic merge-history squashing. Retain source commits before mutation and journal source identities, proven range, target, workspace and replacement. Disable implicit autostash and unrelated ref updates. Verify replacement ancestry, expected change scope and clean Git state before accepting it; record demonstrably already-applied changes explicitly.",
          "verification": [
            "Cover advanced targets, divergent but proven Goal changes, already-applied patches, empty replacement deltas and non-conflict Git failures.",
            "Assert source history remains reachable and unrelated developer changes never enter the replacement."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P4",
          "description": "Make replacement settlement restart-safe through the existing candidate handoff and fenced work-item services. Compare the current attempt, node, Round and old branch/base/candidate before repinning; retain original and replacement identities, proof references and superseded evidence. Reconcile interruptions before replay completion, after local ref replacement, after durable repinning and before journal acknowledgement. Never roll back a durably accepted replacement or overwrite independently changed refs or dirty work. Preserve unresolved transaction evidence when authority or persistence is lost.",
          "verification": [
            "Inject interruption and persistence failures at each settlement boundary, then resume twice to prove idempotency.",
            "Test cancellation, ownership loss, concurrent branch movement and dirty edits during recovery."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P5",
          "description": "Route early lineage repair, the Implement-to-Quality boundary, pre-integration refresh and stale-candidate settlement through the same classifier and replay mechanism. Remove the target-equals-recorded-base shortcut as sufficient proof of an unchanged candidate. Retain integration's ancestry check as a final invariant after repair. For finding retries, materialize a successor workspace from the exact retained candidate, preserve the source checkout and evidence, observe the declared target again and refresh before implementation. Preserve the existing three-pass target-movement limit and shared automatic Round budget across retries and restarts.",
          "verification": [
            "Exercise Quality and Governance recovery after target movement, including missing source checkouts with recoverable committed history.",
            "Verify repeated target movement consumes the existing bounded path without duplicate successor Rounds or reset retry counts."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P6",
          "description": "Preserve supported conflict resolution in the managed replay workspace: retain conflicting paths and snapshots, release the repository lock during resolver work, constrain edits to approved conflict paths, and revalidate authority and the observed target before continuing. Keep disabled/unavailable resolver behavior and shared-budget recovery. Distinguish content conflicts from dirty work, unavailable lineage, authority loss and Git execution errors; none may be reported as successful replay.",
          "verification": [
            "Retain existing resolver, scope-rejection, target-movement and exhaustion coverage.",
            "Add interruption cases proving that only Refine-owned replay operations are recovered and foreign unfinished work remains untouched."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P7",
          "description": "Bind replacement checks to the replacement candidate and current applicable Skill configuration through existing Event and Quality services. Invalidate stale eligibility for Quality proofs, Skill results, Governance verdicts and exit receipts while preserving historical records. Persist candidate-specific invocation identities and configuration snapshots so restart cannot bypass checks or reuse source-candidate results. Rerun applicable Quality and Governance checks after every candidate change. Required bindings gate advancement; background bindings retain their dispatch and workspace rules; context bindings attach without launching. Record explicitly when no required check Skills apply, while still enforcing candidate and integration checks.",
          "verification": [
            "Use deterministic Skill providers to count invocations and assert every replacement receives fresh supervised checks before publication.",
            "Cover required, background, context-only and no-required configurations; configuration changes; correction-created candidates; and restart immediately after repinning.",
            "Preserve valid failed evidence for the same candidate rather than retrying until it passes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "P8",
